dante 1.4.4 libdsocks: reach SOCKS servers over IPv6 from AF_INET sockets

Applies on top of dante-connectchild-workers.patch (and Alpine's ifdev,
gaierrval and dante-no-bindresvport patches). See ipv6-proxy.md.

The program's sockets stay AF_INET and are socksified as before; only the
SOCKS server (via: an IPv6 address, or a name that resolves to IPv6) is
reached over IPv6, for TCP connect (blocking and non-blocking) and UDP
associate.

1. config.c: the client rejected IPv6 gateways ("gateway must be an
   IP-address or qualified domainname"). Allowed now.

2. socks_resocket() (sockopt.c) replaces the socket behind an fd with one of
   the other family, keeping the fd number, type, O_NONBLOCK, FD_CLOEXEC and
   the SOL_SOCKET/IPPROTO_TCP options. IP_TOS/IP_TTL map to IPV6_TCLASS/
   IPV6_UNICAST_HOPS if the program changed them; other IP-level options are
   dropped. A wildcard bind with a fixed port keeps the port; a specific
   (e.g. 127.0.0.1) bind is dropped (logged at debug level).

3. socks_connecthost() (socket.c), client only, so only for gateways:
   - literal gateway of the other family: resocket, then connect;
   - name gateway: resolve both families, try the socket's own family first,
     and resocket for addresses of the other family instead of skipping them.
   Covers blocking connect (the program's fd), non-blocking connect (the
   control socket, dup2()ed onto the program's fd by sigio(); the AF_INET
   dummy fd is bound to 127.0.0.1 then) and the UDP control connection,
   which is now created with the gateway's family.

4. UDP data socket (udp.c): resocketed to the control connection's family
   before the UDP ASSOCIATE request, so the announced address matches, and
   again if the relay address is of the other family. udpsetup() recognises
   the replaced socket on later calls. Rrecvfrom() converts IPv4-mapped
   sources to AF_INET and drops datagrams whose source the program's
   AF_INET socket can not represent (debug log).

5. What the program sees: socksfd_t.origfamily records the program's family.
   Rgetsockname() returns 0.0.0.0 with the BND port for an IPv6 BND.ADDR
   instead of a truncated sockaddr_in6. socks_addrisours() handles IPv6
   local addresses (it read sin_addr of a sockaddr_in6). getsockopt
   (SO_DOMAIN) shows AF_INET6 on a replaced fd; IPv4-level setsockopt()s
   after connect are accepted by Linux but only affect IPv4-mapped traffic.

Test: test/run.sh (test/v6check.c).

